<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beijing</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beijing is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> that has served as the capital of several imperial dynasties. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khanbaliq">Khanbaliq</a>) it was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> moved its capital there in the early fifteenth century, building the Forbidden City. Its fall to rebels and then to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchus</a> in 1644 marked the end of the Ming and the foundation of Qing rule in China.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beijing.jpg" alt="Beijing" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: N509FZ · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skyline_of_Beijing_CBD_with_B-5906_approaching_(20211016171955)_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
